<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Jose Paredes</title><link>https://jparedesds.com/en/</link><description>Recent content on Jose Paredes</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><managingEditor>jparedescolmenarejo@gmail.com (Jose Paredes)</managingEditor><webMaster>jparedescolmenarejo@gmail.com (Jose Paredes)</webMaster><lastBuildDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0100</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://jparedesds.com/en/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Detecting welding defects with YOLO11x</title><link>https://jparedesds.com/en/blog/2026/11/23/welding-defects-detection/</link><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0100</pubDate><author>jparedescolmenarejo@gmail.com (Jose Paredes)</author><guid>https://jparedesds.com/en/blog/2026/11/23/welding-defects-detection/</guid><description>A weld seam, a workpiece, porosity and a catch-all Defect class: four things a single YOLO11x detector learns to localise. The structure and porosity work well; the long tail of defect morphologies is the real problem.</description></item><item><title>About</title><link>https://jparedesds.com/en/about/</link><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><author>jparedescolmenarejo@gmail.com (Jose Paredes)</author><guid>https://jparedesds.com/en/about/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;I am a computer vision and ML engineer based in Madrid. At &lt;a href="https://www.eipsa.es/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;EIPSA&lt;/a&gt; I build computer vision systems and data automation for industrial engineering, from inspection models on the production line to the tooling that surrounds them. Outside of work I build local-first AI products: tools that run on your own machine and keep your data there.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Resume: &lt;a href="https://jparedesds.com/resume.pdf"&gt;PDF&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Languages: Spanish (native) · English (B2)&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id="projects"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2&gt;Projects&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://subany.video/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Subany&lt;/a&gt; — live subtitles in the browser. Whisper and ONNX on WebGPU, with no server round-trip.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://subany.site/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;subany.site&lt;/a&gt; — the project site for subany.video.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.cleanyourmail.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;CleanYourMail&lt;/a&gt; — a local-first way to clean up a Gmail inbox without handing over your mail.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.cleanyourphone.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;CleanYourPhone&lt;/a&gt; — the same idea for your phone: inspect and clean it locally.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/jparedesDS/docflow" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;DocFlow&lt;/a&gt; — document automation for industrial teams.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://propovcs2.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Pro POV CS2&lt;/a&gt; — a computer-vision project for Counter-Strike 2 POV clips.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/jparedesDS" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;GitHub&lt;/a&gt; — the rest of the code, including the models published on Hugging Face.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="open-projects"&gt;Open projects&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Every repository and model is listed on the dedicated &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://jparedesds.com/en/repositories/"&gt;Repositories&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; page.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Archive</title><link>https://jparedesds.com/en/blog/archives/</link><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><author>jparedescolmenarejo@gmail.com (Jose Paredes)</author><guid>https://jparedesds.com/en/blog/archives/</guid><description/></item><item><title>FAQ</title><link>https://jparedesds.com/en/blog/faq/</link><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><author>jparedescolmenarejo@gmail.com (Jose Paredes)</author><guid>https://jparedesds.com/en/blog/faq/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="who-are-you"&gt;Who are you?&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;I&amp;rsquo;m Jose Paredes, a computer vision and ML engineer in Madrid. I build computer-vision&#10;systems, automation and local-first products.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="what-do-you-write-about"&gt;What do you write about?&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Data, computer vision, automation and local-first AI products: how they work, the&#10;trade-offs behind them and the parts that were hard to get right.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="can-i-use-the-code"&gt;Can I use the code?&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Yes. The snippets are there to be reused; if a post links to a repository, check that&#10;repository&amp;rsquo;s licence first. Attribution is appreciated but not required.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>How subany.video works: live subtitles in the browser</title><link>https://jparedesds.com/en/blog/2026/11/09/how-subany-video-works/</link><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0100</pubDate><author>jparedescolmenarejo@gmail.com (Jose Paredes)</author><guid>https://jparedesds.com/en/blog/2026/11/09/how-subany-video-works/</guid><description>subany.video is a small experiment with a deliberately narrow promise: paste a Twitch link and watch the stream with translated subtitles. The video, the speech recognition and the translation all run in the browser.</description></item><item><title>Contact</title><link>https://jparedesds.com/en/contact/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><author>jparedescolmenarejo@gmail.com (Jose Paredes)</author><guid>https://jparedesds.com/en/contact/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Madrid · Open to opportunities.&lt;/strong&gt; I’m open to select AI, computer-vision and local-first product work.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Email: &lt